## Product Analysis

![Product Analysis](Product Analysis.png)

This dashboard analyses product-level performance using the transformed retail dataset integrated from SQL into Power BI.

The goal of this analysis was to understand how revenue is distributed across products and identify which items drive the majority of sales.

Key metrics displayed include:

• **Total Product Revenue** – total revenue generated across all products  
• **Total Units Sold** – overall product sales volume  
• **Average Revenue per Product** – average contribution of each product to total revenue  

The **Product Revenue vs Units Sold scatter plot** highlights the relationship between product demand and revenue contribution. This helps identify:

- high-volume products generating consistent revenue  
- premium products generating high revenue with lower sales volume  
- underperforming products with low demand and revenue  

The **product revenue distribution chart** shows that sales are concentrated among a relatively small number of products. A few high-performing items generate a disproportionate share of revenue, while the majority of products contribute smaller individual amounts.

The **product performance table** provides a detailed ranking of items by revenue and units sold, enabling quick identification of top-selling and high-value products.

This analysis demonstrates how Power BI can be used to identify key revenue drivers, support product strategy decisions, and highlight opportunities for inventory or marketing optimisation.
